# Allocation stability check (not an exact count). The host driver counts live
# malloc blocks, lets the task queue drain, samples the net delta, waits a quiet
# window and samples again. Both samples must match, so a leaked payload or
# child handle shows up as growth. The queue backing buffer is an accepted
# startup cost, so its concrete allocator value is never pinned. An optional
# `max <n>` line would add an upper bound.
